          A straight line passes through the origin and extends diagonally across the coordinate space.  
          </description>
        </image>
    </statement>
  </exercise>
<exercise xml:id="ex-plot-points-3d-ex-2">
    <statement>
        <p>
    Plot the point <m>(1,2,4)</m> in three-dimensional space.
  </p>
<image source="images/ch01/ThreeDCoordinateGrid.png">
          <description>
          A three-dimensional coordinate system is shown with horizontal, vertical, and depth axes labeled x, y, and z.
          A straight line passes through the origin and extends diagonally across the coordinate space.  
          </description>
